### 🧪 Add Test Case for JSON Error Body Extraction

To ensure that `postJson` correctly extracts and throws structured error messages from non-OK JSON responses, we should add a corresponding unit test case.

```typescript
		it('throws on non-OK HTTP status', async () => {
			const mockResponse = {
				ok: false,
				status: 500,
				statusText: 'Internal Server Error'
			} as unknown as Response;

			vi.stubGlobal(
				'fetch',
				vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(mockResponse)
			);

			await expect(postJson('/api/test', {})).rejects.toThrow(
				'postJson: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error'
			);
		});

		it('throws on non-OK HTTP status and extracts JSON error message if available', async () => {
			const mockResponse = {
				ok: false,
				status: 400,
				statusText: 'Bad Request',
				json: () => Promise.resolve({ error: { message: 'Custom API Error' } })
			} as unknown as Response;

			vi.stubGlobal(
				'fetch',
				vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(mockResponse)
			);

			await expect(postJson('/api/test', {})).rejects.toThrow(
				'Custom API Error'
			);
		});
```
